body:sub(1, analysis_start - 1) .. new_analysis_text .. body:sub(analysis_end + 1)\n./reascript/vgt_read_chords.lua:348:  -- would block headless/automated runs waiting for a click that never\n./docs/GOAL.md:50:### Phase 1 — Reference analysis *(current)*\n./docs/GOAL.md:60:- **an analysis stage in the CLI** — heavy analysis runs in the Python CLI, never inside REAPER; the ReaScript\n./docs/GOAL.md:62:- **persisting analysis in the sidecar** — extend the `<project>.vgt` schema (bump `schema_version`) to hold the\n./docs/GOAL.md:64:- **reflecting analysis into the project**, additively and idempotently, as `[vgt]`-owned objects:\n./docs/GOAL.md:69:    timeline and read back into the sidecar as human-verified corrections (see README's \"Correcting chords in\n./docs/GOAL.md:74:[phase1-song-prep-plan.md](phase1-song-prep-plan.md) is the longer-range roadmap; phase 1 here is its analysis\n./docs/GOAL.md:88:- **Analysis stays out of the DAW process.** ML/DSP analysis runs in the Python CLI; REAPER only reads the\n./docs/GOAL.md:89:  reference source path and applies results through the API. The DAW never loads heavy analysis dependencies.\n./docs/GOAL.md:90:- **Correctable.** Auto-analysis will sometimes be wrong; every detected value (tempo, key, sections, chords) is\n./docs/GOAL.md:91:  overridable, and corrections survive re-runs of the analysis.\n./reascript/vgt_initialize.lua:98:-- The Python `vgt analyze` stage (schema v2) adds a top-level \"analysis\"\n./reascript/vgt_initialize.lua:101:-- rather than silently dropping any analysis a user has already run.\n./reascript/vgt_initialize.lua:102:local function read_analysis_block()\n./reascript/vgt_initialize.lua:105:  local key_start = body:find('\"analysis\"%s*:%s*{')\n./reascript/vgt_initialize.lua:228:local function read_analysis()\n./reascript/vgt_initialize.lua:229:  local block = read_analysis_block()\n./reascript/vgt_initialize.lua:286:  -- unlocked (locked == false) so the user can correct them on the timeline;